    <Label IsHitTestVisible="false" Name="Title" Style="GalleryTitle" Text="Cavalieri's Principle" DecimalsToShow="2" X="5.659" Y="-0.979" />
    <Label IsHitTestVisible="false" Name="Description" Style="GalleryText" Text="The area of a triangle is ½ · base · height.\nWhy doesn't it matter where the top is?\n\nThink of the triangle as a stack of thin\nslices. Slide the top sideways: every slice\nmoves but keeps its length, so the area stays\nthe same.\n\nDrag the top vertex." DecimalsToShow="2" X="5.659" Y="-1.788" />
